MODE      cm-threads-spawn-parked
FORMS     0x27 thread.new-indirect (and task.return), with the created Thread NEVER readied
RESULT    2
EXIT      0
RUNS      3, identical

WHAT IT PINS
  The created Thread's index is 2, with the implicit Thread at 1 — the reference's Table policy.
  The call RETURNS with that Thread still registered and never started: its body is `unreachable`
  and did not trap, so it did not run. That is legal in the reference — unregister_thread constrains
  only the LAST Thread's exit to follow resolution, and Threads outlive resolution (ADR 0100).

WHY IT EXISTS
  It is the subject of ADR 0100's parked-Thread wake. In this engine a created Thread is a goroutine
  parked in a Go select. Neither reclamation path reaches it: interp.ErrClosed needs the goroutine to
  RE-ENTER through invokeIndex, and interp.ErrTerminated needs it at a SAFEPOINT running guest code. A
  parked Thread is at neither, so Close must wake it explicitly. The wasmtime reading pins only the
  index and the fact that the body never runs; the wake itself is engine-internal and witnessed by
  TestCloseEndsAParkedThreadsGoroutine.

